Ways the change could fail a criterion (what each rating is measured against):

  context-section-optional-background
    [scope_too_narrow] context-section-optional-background/subheading-in-context-escapes-section
      Every heading node, at any level, resets `section`. A `### Measurements` or `### Today's behaviour` sub-heading inside `## Context` therefore ends the context section. The blocks after it go to `unclaimed`, or to behavior or constraints if the sub-heading name matches one of those. Background content is then not treated as context and can be read as mandate.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 110 skipped once the defect was covered
    [not_wired] context-section-optional-background/context-not-counted-as-read-source
      A `context` field was added to `ParsedTaskFile`, but the change does not show the unread-source and total-coverage accounting being updated. If that accounting sums only the old lists, Context blocks are reported as unread or uncovered, or the file is rejected or flagged. A task file with a Context section would then not be cleanly accepted.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#2
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#3
      pairs: 60 put to the model, 54 skipped once the defect was covered
    [other] context-section-optional-background/context-block-obligation-not-rejected
      Context is shown to the decomposer only with a prompt instruction not to derive obligations from it. Nothing in the delivered code stops the model from returning an obligation that restates Context text, for example current behaviour that must be kept. If the quote check also accepts text from Context, background can still become an obligation.
      src/acceptance/requirement/obligations.py#3
      src/acceptance/requirement/obligations.py#5
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 110 skipped once the defect was covered
    [not_wired] context-section-optional-background/context-not-passed-on-some-decompose-path
      Context is threaded through `_ask_about` at only two call sites. Any other decomposition or retry path that builds the prompt without `parsed.context` would silently drop the background, or would behave differently with and without the section.
      src/acceptance/requirement/obligations.py#6
      src/acceptance/requirement/obligations.py#7
      src/acceptance/requirement/obligations.py#1
      pairs: 1 put to the model, 0 skipped once the defect was covered

  parse-records-context-field
    [scope_too_narrow] parse-records-context-field/subheading-ends-context-section
      Every heading, at any level, resets `section`. A `### Measurements` subheading inside `## Context` therefore ends the Context section. Blocks after it are not recorded in `context` and probably fall to `unclaimed`, so only the content before the first subheading is captured.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      pairs: 12 put to the model, 102 skipped once the defect was covered
    [missing_case] parse-records-context-field/context-heading-match-exact
      The Context section is recognised only when the lowercased heading text equals exactly `context`. Variants such as `Context:` or `Background` do not match, so that content is not recorded in `context`. The heading level is not checked at all, so a `# Context` heading also matches.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#1
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 110 skipped once the defect was covered
    [other] parse-records-context-field/container-blocks-in-context-mishandled
      The Context branch handles each node as paragraph, list, or 'anything else', and the 'anything else' case goes to `_block_span`. Container nodes such as blockquotes are meant to be descended into rather than spanned. If a container reaches this branch it would be spanned whole, or its inner blocks might not be captured. That would break the total-coverage property, so the `context` content would be wrong in shape.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#1
      pairs: 5 put to the model, 109 skipped once the defect was covered

  context-blocks-carry-source-spans
    [scope_too_narrow] context-blocks-carry-source-spans/subheading-ends-context-section
      Any heading inside the Context section, such as a `### Measurements` subheading, replaces `section` with that heading's text. Blocks after it are no longer in `_CONTEXT`. They go to `unclaimed` or another list, so the recorded Context field misses blocks that belong to the Context section.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 110 skipped once the defect was covered
    [other] context-blocks-carry-source-spans/non-paragraph-block-span-wrong
      Non-paragraph, non-list Context blocks (tables, fenced code, quotes) are spanned by `_block_span`, a different helper from the `_span` used for paragraphs. If it computes offsets or lines differently, for example by ignoring `line_offsets`, the span may not map back to the block's real position in the file.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 110 skipped once the defect was covered
    [wrong_output_shape] context-blocks-carry-source-spans/context-list-items-span-granularity
      List blocks in Context go through `_emit_list`, which may emit spans per item. If it flattens or skips nested lists or items, or emits one span for the whole list, the Context blocks may not match the block unit used elsewhere. Some nested content may then have no span or an imprecise one.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#3
      pairs: 1 put to the model, 0 skipped once the defect was covered
    [missing_case] context-blocks-carry-source-spans/container-nodes-in-context-skipped
      The context branch is checked per node of the walk. Container nodes such as blockquotes are descended into rather than spanned. A blockquote or other container inside Context may be walked in a way that skips its inner blocks or spans them wrongly. Those inner blocks would then be absent from `context` or lack correct spans.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#1
      pairs: 5 put to the model, 109 skipped once the defect was covered

  context-not-reported-unread
